{"id":"000VJQ","title":"Rainfall","author":"sisaloofafump","solvedCount":1,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-20T18:30:50+00:00","posted":"Heute, 20:09 Uhr","rules":"Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\nThermometers: Digits decrease from tip to bulb.\n\nUnique: Each bulb has a unique number.\n\nOutside numbers: Each number outside the grid is located n cells down the column/row it is next to, where n is the first digit along the column/row. (For example, if the outside digit is 6, and the inside digit it is next to is 3, then the digit 6 in that row is 3 cells away from that edge.)\n\nIf anyone knows a better name for the outside number system, let me know! SudokuMaker calls them \"numbered rooms\" but i dont see that used on this site.\n\nPlay on SudokuPad","solutionCode":"Column 9, top to bottom","tags":["Sudoku","Thermometer","Extra Regions (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/vq6cqvin2p","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/vq6cqvin2p","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-20T18:30:50+00:00"}